Capacity Reconciliation

Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs

Capacity Reconciliation is an open-source, vendor-neutral runtime for
deterministic reconciliation and discrepancy classification across planned,
reserved, installed, observed, usable and allocatable facility capacity views.
It is built from the C++20 standard library only.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the
LICENSE file in this distribution for the full license text.

Capacity Reconciliation does not collect or transmit any telemetry. It makes no
network connection of any kind. Every byte it writes goes to the local store
directory the operator names on the command line or passes to the library, and
nothing leaves the machine running the software.

Capacity Reconciliation accepts contributions from individuals and organizations
on the terms of the Apache License 2.0 without requiring a Contributor License
Agreement (CLA). See CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution guidance.

Third-party components
----------------------

None. No third-party source code, library, header or generated artefact is
included in, linked into, or required by this product.

The build depends only on the platform's own toolchain and operating system:

  * the C++20 standard library of the toolchain that builds the project;
  * the operating system's cryptographic random generator, used for identity
    and store-identity entropy and reached through the platform API
    (BCryptGenRandom on Windows, the platform entropy source elsewhere);
  * the operating system's file, locking and durability primitives, used for
    the durable store and for writer fencing.

No network service, telemetry endpoint, analytics library or runtime package
manager is contacted or required at build time or at run time.

